      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Another useful matrix operation is transposition. The transpose of a matrix A is written $ \\mathbf{A}^T $ (while not used in this book, the notation $ \\mathbf{A}' $ is also widely used), and is obtained simply by switching rows and columns of the original matrix. For example,",
